# 2. The biggest opportunity: a Neuro Tumor State

I would build the entire platform around one persistent data structure:

```text
PATIENT
   │
   └── NEURO TUMOR EPISODE
         │
         ├── Diagnosis / WHO state
         ├── Molecular state
         ├── Pathology
         ├── Imaging timeline
         │     ├── MRI
         │     ├── PET
         │     ├── Perfusion
         │     ├── Diffusion
         │     └── Spectroscopy
         │
         ├── Lesion graph
         │     ├── Lesion #001
         │     ├── Lesion #002
         │     └── Lesion #003
         │
         ├── Surgery
         ├── Radiation
         ├── Systemic therapy
         ├── Steroids / supportive treatment
         ├── Neurologic state
         ├── RANO state
         ├── Treatment-response state
         ├── Evidence state
         ├── Trial eligibility
         └── Outcome trajectory
```

That becomes the platform's **single source of truth**.

Every new MRI updates the state.

Every pathology result updates the state.

Every mutation updates the state.

Every therapy updates the state.

Every new lesion gets an identity.

Every response assessment gets a timepoint.

Every AI prediction gets attached to the evidence that produced it.

That is much harder to replicate than an isolated segmentation model.

