# 5. Module #3 — Lesion Identity Graph

This is particularly powerful for brain metastases.

Instead of storing:

> MRI report, Jan 1
> MRI report, Mar 3
> MRI report, May 4

you store:

```text
LESION 001
 ├── first detected
 ├── coordinates
 ├── size trajectory
 ├── treatment
 ├── RT dose
 ├── response
 ├── recurrence
 └── current state

LESION 002
 ├── first detected
 ├── treated with SRS
 ├── shrank
 ├── regrew
 └── radiation-effect probability

LESION 003
 ├── new
 ├── never irradiated
 └── untreated
```

This addresses a real documented problem: longitudinal reports lose lesion identity as cases become complex. ([PubMed][3])

A clinician should be able to click **Lesion 002** and see its entire history.

That is a major product concept.

