# 6. Module #4 — MRI Quality & Harmonization Layer

This is less sexy than AI diagnosis but potentially very valuable.

Before the model interprets a scan, the platform should ask:

```text
Can this scan safely be compared with prior imaging?
```

Check:

* scanner vendor
* field strength
* sequence
* voxel size
* slice thickness
* contrast timing
* motion
* signal quality
* distortion
* missing sequences
* acquisition changes

Then generate:

### Imaging comparability score

```text
LONGITUDINAL COMPARABILITY

T1 CE ............ 94%
FLAIR ............ 87%
DWI .............. 61%
Perfusion ........ 72%

Overall: MODERATE
```

The software could then warn:

> "Apparent change may be influenced by acquisition differences."

This matters because scanner-related variation is a recognized obstacle in longitudinal neuroimaging and multicenter AI development. ([Nature][5])

