# 10. Module #8 — Evidence Engine

This fits very naturally into what you're already building.

The clinician should be able to ask:

> "Why is the system calling this indeterminate?"

and get:

```text
Patient evidence
↓
Imaging evidence
↓
Treatment context
↓
Molecular evidence
↓
Relevant RANO criteria
↓
Published evidence
↓
Clinical trials
```

Every AI conclusion should have a **source/evidence trail**.

That is especially important because current research increasingly favors multimodal AI, but the gap between benchmark performance and safe real-world clinical usefulness remains substantial. A 2026 Nature Biomedical Engineering review specifically emphasizes data scarcity, domain heterogeneity, interpretability, workflow integration and safety as major barriers for biomedical foundation models. ([Nature][15])

So don't build:

> "ChatGPT for neuro-oncology."

Build:

> **Evidence-linked neuro-oncology reasoning infrastructure.**

