# 11. Module #9 — Dynamic Tumor Biology

This is where your longer-term research moat becomes interesting.

The tumor should not be represented as:

> "Glioblastoma."

It should become:

```text
CURRENT STATE

Clone
State
Location
Microenvironment
Treatment pressure
Imaging phenotype
Molecular phenotype
Response phenotype
```

This is consistent with the direction of current GBM research. Spatial/single-cell studies increasingly show multiple malignant cellular communities and distinct microenvironments rather than a single homogeneous tumor. ([Nature][8])

Your software could eventually construct:

### Tumor habitats

```text
Habitat A
high perfusion
high cellularity
enhancing

Habitat B
hypoxic
necrotic
low perfusion

Habitat C
infiltrative
FLAIR dominant
non-enhancing
```

Then connect those regions to:

* pathology
* molecular state
* treatment exposure
* recurrence
* spatial transcriptomics
* radiomics

That starts turning imaging into a **map of tumor evolution**, not merely a picture.

