# 17. Where the field appears to be heading

The direction is becoming unusually clear.

In September 2026, IARC announced the EUcanAI project, a four-year effort to build networked AI systems specialized across brain-tumor care steps including consultation, diagnosis and therapy. ([IARC][19])

EANO 2026 is also occurring **right now, September 24–27, 2026**, bringing together neuro-oncology, neurosurgery, neuropathology, neuroradiology, radiation oncology and other disciplines around precision diagnostics and management. ([EANO][20])

So the strategic opening is not:

> "Can AI segment a brain tumor?"

That problem is already being solved.

It is:

> **Can software maintain a living, evidence-linked model of the patient's brain tumor across time and across specialties?**

That is the product I would build.

